    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nIf 'complete' has the \"u\" flag, mini.complete autocompletion can be very slow.\n\n## Suggestion\n\nIn the mini-completion.txt, it would save users time if there is a \"Performance\" section that suggests `set complete-=u`. I see that the `# Suggested option values` section has a similar note about the \"t\" flag, but `:help mini.completion` has no results when searching for \"slow\" or \"perf\", and this might result in users giving up instead of figuring out when 'complete' flag (if they even know about that) is causing an issue.\n\nSide-note:\n- some skeleton of tips on performance troubleshooting might be worthwhile.\n- the \"u\" performance (and visibility thereof) is probably something Neovim itself should think about, since it's a default, and a rather annoying trap...",
